  "investigation_notes": "Uploads are failing because the app's database dependency is down - not storage.\n\n* App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 4 seconds` while DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `exited` `Exited (0) 2 seconds ago` [E1]. App `/health` is `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` [E2].\n* App container: `running:true, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false`, user `1000:1000`, mount `source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true`, network `incidentlab_default` [E4].\n* DB container: `running:false, status:exited, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false`, `health:unhealthy`, same network `incidentlab_default` [E5].\n* App logs for both `upload` in `/app/main.py line 65` and `health` in `/app/main.py line 113` show same symptom:\n  `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` [E6][E12].\n  This is expected when the `db` container is not running on that network, not a primary app bug.\n* DB logs show healthy start then clean external shutdown, not a crash:\n  `database system is ready to accept connections` then `received fast shutdown request`, `shutting down`, `checkpoint complete`, `database system is shut down` [E7], with `older_lines_omitted:0` showing full history.\n* Docker events show repeated external `kill/stop/die exit 0` for `incidentlab-db-1`, including isolated `kill/stop/die` at `23:57:32` and `23:58:20`, plus recreate sequences `create/kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start` at `23:57:24` and `23:58:12` [E3]. `exit_code 0` + `oom_killed:false` [E5] rules out OOM/crash as cause of stop.\n\nStorage causes ruled out for upload path `/srv/lab-data/uploads` bind-mounted as `/data`:\n\n* Filesystem `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent:9.0, inode_use_percent:0.2` [E8]. Root `/`: `use_percent:6.8, inode_use_percent:1.5` [E9] - not full.\n* `/srv/lab-data/uploads`: `is_dir:true, owner 1000:1000, mode 0755, app 1000:1000, app_user_can_write:true` [E10].\n* `/srv/lab-data`: `is_dir:true, owner 1000:1000, mode 0755, app 1000:1000, app_user_can_write:true` [E11], matching app user [E4] with `rw:true` mount [E4].\n* No `Permission denied` / `No space left` / file-write errors in app logs, only DB resolution errors [E6][E12].\n\nRoot cause vs symptom: root cause is `incidentlab-db-1` stopped via clean shutdown [E5][E7][E3]; app `503` [E2] and `upload` `OperationalError` [E6] are symptoms of that dependency loss. Why the stop was issued is not shown - no evidence of OOM [E5], disk full [E8][E9], or DB internal error [E7].\n",
